From f94f969d4ae95d6d6b560bd3dfe5b25debbfc75e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:26:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/46] game: call the side-effecting initialisers directly
 instead of through an UNUSED local

`UNUSED f32 sp30 = random_float();` is there for the call, not the value:
the RNG must advance, `object_step()` must move the object, `find_floor`
must run. Writing the call as a statement says so; the dead local said
the opposite.

Verified: each file, through its including translation unit, compiles to
byte-identical assembly before and after with the port's own flags
(asmdiff over compile_commands.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game/behaviors/bowling_ball.inc.c | 2 +-
 src/game/behaviors/end_birds_1.inc.c  | 3 ++-
 src/game/behaviors/end_birds_2.inc.c  | 2 +-
 src/game/behaviors/red_coin.inc.c     | 2 +-
 src/game/behaviors/snowman.inc.c      | 2 +-
 5 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

